 ## Operating characteristics
-* Time Complexity: Rendering is $O(N \cdot S)$ per pixel, where $N$ is the number of samples per ray and $S$ is the number of rays (pixels). The warping function adds overhead for coordinate transformation and volume interpolation [S1].
-* Memory Complexity: The volume representation requires memory proportional to the resolution of the voxel grids. For a $128^3$ volume with 8 channels, this is significant but manageable. The warping grid adds $32^3 \times 16$ channels [S1].
+* Time Complexity: Not given in the sources.
+* Memory Complexity: Not given in the sources.
 * Strengths: Handles complex materials (high glossiness) and accurate hard shadows under novel lighting, which mesh-based methods and standard volume rendering struggle with [S1]. Editable reflectance volumes allow material editing [S1].
-* Limitations: Limited to single-bounce light transport. Performance is sensitive to the step size $\Delta x$ and the learned warping function. Requires per-scene optimization [S1].
+* Limitations: Limited to single-bounce light transport. Requires per-scene optimization [S1].
 
